  "additional_visual_samples": {
    "samples": [
      {
        "lesson": "01_pypi_github",
        "scene": 5,
        "at_seconds": 76.20568662384879,
        "path": "/mnt/firecuda2/Claude/toxoplasma_projects/tutorials/refresh_2026-09-09/web-renditions/01_pypi_github/review-midpoint.jpg",
        "text": "Open a release and expand Assets. Match the installer to Windows, macOS or Linux. The wheel and source distribution are Python package files, not desktop installers. Download the checksum list for the exact release and file you selected, rather than comparing hashes from another channel.",
        "sha256": "cf055cae6acd9ea8df0a6ade12dbe3bb1b4bdbe6bd07919b9eda4ee564910159",
        "visually_inspected": true
      },
      {
        "lesson": "07_mask",
        "scene": 9,
        "at_seconds": 176.6973627259295,
        "path": "/mnt/firecuda2/Claude/toxoplasma_projects/tutorials/refresh_2026-09-09/web-renditions/07_mask/review-midpoint.jpg",
        "text": "For the separate batch, use two test images and keep Plot enabled. Here all three flow thresholds are explicitly zero point four. The downloaded settings had one hundred, which disables flow filtering; we do not recommend that value by default. Review the console's device and processing messages instead of assuming how the run executed.",
        "sha256": "a54ed3952ed9cf3538b77640ba9cdc54699a0c0684263e96c761cb7f744d6b73",
        "visually_inspected": true
      },
      {
        "lesson": "08_measure",
        "scene": 7,
        "at_seconds": 133.0679931916381,
        "path": "/mnt/firecuda2/Claude/toxoplasma_projects/tutorials/refresh_2026-09-09/web-renditions/08_measure/review-midpoint.jpg",
        "text": "Turn Live off, search for Normalize again, and switch it off before running. We verified that all batch settings return to their original values and both source arrays remain unchanged. Per-crop normalization can remove intensity differences from saved images. Keep the original arrays; this lesson does not use the oversized Crop settings dialog.",
        "sha256": "a1215a334861b0f43855eb6db1315aedd9081d1ac9beede7a703eb76d7d43f1d",
        "visually_inspected": true
      },
      {
        "lesson": "10_classify_cv",
        "scene": 7,
        "at_seconds": 136.33713042479997,
        "path": "/mnt/firecuda2/Claude/toxoplasma_projects/tutorials/refresh_2026-09-09/web-renditions/10_classify_cv/review-midpoint.jpg",
        "text": "Choose ResNet18 for this bounded example: one epoch, batches of eight, image size one hundred twenty-eight, and zero loader workers. Use all three RGB channels and leave pretrained weights and augmentation off. These settings make the demonstration small; they are not a recommended recipe for an accurate classifier.",
        "sha256": "b15578d431826a7b999f4e99fbd78bdf987999ca97e385ea181df4722991187e",
        "visually_inspected": true
      }
    ],
    "scope": "Four additional decoded 1440p scene midpoints, not a complete-frame audit",
    "published": false
  },
  "result_view_samples": {
    "samples": [
      {
        "lesson": "13_regression",
        "scene": 16,
        "at_seconds": 278.1591645129063,
        "path": "/mnt/firecuda2/Claude/toxoplasma_projects/tutorials/refresh_2026-09-09/web-renditions/13_regression/review-results.jpg",
        "text": "Open the p-values view to inspect the result distribution. Interpret it together with the selected testing family, permutation resolution and diagnostics, not as automatic evidence of an effect. The separate Diagnostics tutorial explains the saved design and inference panels in detail.",
        "sha256": "a7d43f4fce4314874d78e70798f9ec30035bd68b12839dd15ebb917afe98e07d",
        "visually_inspected": true
      },
      {
        "lesson": "15_image_umap",
        "scene": 13,
        "at_seconds": 200.0470712367256,
        "path": "/mnt/firecuda2/Claude/toxoplasma_projects/tutorials/refresh_2026-09-09/web-renditions/15_image_umap/review-results.jpg",
        "text": "Turn on Interactive to explore the already fitted map. This is not a live refit of changing settings. Clicking points, zooming and selecting regions helps inspect the current result; changing the analysis still requires another run.",
        "sha256": "f0d5f5d80042081020e4c9e21432dc86ad83ba28611e337462c88e88e8963e78",
        "visually_inspected": true
      },
      {
        "lesson": "24_plaque",
        "scene": 9,
        "at_seconds": 159.2459183450608,
        "path": "/mnt/firecuda2/Claude/toxoplasma_projects/tutorials/refresh_2026-09-09/web-renditions/24_plaque/review-results.jpg",
        "text": "In Live settings, raise Min area to twenty-six thousand two hundred eleven pixels. This removes the two smaller predicted objects. The filtering reuses cached masks rather than running the model again. Change one setting at a time so you can see which objects it removes.",
        "sha256": "be14f5ac64b4bdb2577b60dcce31793e32831fd7a4d1f5f3b98176fb6fbbf0a6",
        "visually_inspected": true
      },
      {
        "lesson": "25_recruitment",
        "scene": 14,
        "at_seconds": 259.48328539469475,
        "path": "/mnt/firecuda2/Claude/toxoplasma_projects/tutorials/refresh_2026-09-09/web-renditions/25_recruitment/review-results.jpg",
        "text": "Inspect the real archived image and its stored mask overlay. Its label areas differ from the measurement table. Recorded filtering and merging can explain that difference, but we have not reconstructed the exact historical masks. The overlay is context, not proof that an individual displayed boundary produced a particular recruitment ratio.",
        "sha256": "b95a5409a450961176db21df084d64ed17cc094e5a84b474558a8d231d857e3c",
